  "claim": "Dieppe Raid is the name of the military engagement on the northern coast of France on 19 August 1942 in which the HMS \"Calpe\" participated.",
  "evidencia": "Page: HMS Calpe (L71). Sentence: HMS \"Calpe\" (pennant number L71) was a British Royal Navy Type II Hunt-class destroyer escort.\nPage: HMS Calpe (L71). Sentence: Built as a result of the outbreak of World War II, \"Calpe\" escorted convoys during the war and participated in the Dieppe Raid.\nPage: Dieppe Raid. Sentence: The Dieppe Raid, also known as the Battle of Dieppe, Operation \"Rutter during planning stages, and by its final official code-name Operation \"Jubilee, was an Allied attack on the German-occupied port of Dieppe during the Second World War.\nPage: Dieppe Raid. Sentence: The raid took place on the northern coast of France on 19 August 1942.",
