        "original_id": "800f5272-b1ce-55f1-b582-696f8435eeb9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Ships: HMS Calpe (L71)\n- Organizations: Royal Navy, Allied forces\n- Operations and Events: Dieppe Raid, Battle of Dieppe, Operation Rutter, Operation Jubilee, World War II\n- Places: Dieppe, northern coast of France\n\nFacts:\n- HMS Calpe (L71) was built as a result of the outbreak of World War II.\n- HMS Calpe (L71) was a British Royal Navy Type II Hunt-class destroyer escort.\n- During World War II, HMS Calpe (L71) escorted convoys and participated in the Dieppe Raid.\n- The Dieppe Raid was also known as the Battle of Dieppe, Operation Rutter during planning stages, and Operation Jubilee as its final official code-name.\n- The Dieppe Raid was an Allied attack on the German-occupied port of Dieppe during the Second World War.\n- The Dieppe Raid took place on the northern coast of France on 19 August 1942.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
